{{!--
  THE CARD UNDER A TILE (D-738).

  TEXT ONLY. It is rendered once per tile into `tile.tipHtml` and handed to
  core through `data-tooltip-html`, which passes it through
  `foundry.utils.cleanHTML` (14.367) — a `class` survives that and an event
  handler does not, so nothing here may be a control.

  `rules/bags.mjs#tipModel` composes every line; the words arrive localised in
  a bag (D-677) because that module is pure. **The rarity and the kind are
  said in WORDS**, so the tile's ring is never the only carrier (D5), and a
  line with nothing to say is left out rather than drawn empty.
--}}
<div class="azeroth-item-tip-body">
  <p class="azeroth-item-tip-name{{#if tip.rarityClass}} {{tip.rarityClass}}{{/if}}">{{tip.name}}</p>
  {{#each tip.lines as |line|}}
  <p class="azeroth-item-tip-line is-{{line.key}}">{{line.text}}</p>
  {{/each}}
</div>
